# The Shadower's first job node: four dashes through the crowd, each slashing
# everything it passes.
#
# GMS's own figures: 720+20x% six times on twelve enemies, four presses to a
# 60s cooldown. The client carries an id per dash -- 400041002 chains through
# 400041003-5, all three `invisible` -- and the 6th job boost lifts the count
# from 4, which is what settles the number the tooltip muddles as "2-4".
#
# One press here, charged all four dashes: 420ms of frames apiece, and
# `cast_interval_ms` tells them apart on that same beat so each finds the crowd
# as it then stands rather than piling four landings onto one group of twelve.
# The three follow-ups fall inside the 1680ms the press costs, so nothing is
# had for free.
#
# The crit rate and the DEF it ignores ride this swing alone, as GMS states
# them. Dropped: the 300 MP, the immunity while dashing, and the direction of
# the dash -- nothing here has a place to be.
name: "Shadow Assault"
description: "Instantly move to slash enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_SHADOWER_V skill_order: 1 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_DAGGER
base_delay_ms: 1680
cooldown_seconds: 60.0
max_enemies: 12
lines: 6
casts: 4
cast_interval_ms: 420
base {
  skill_pct: 7.40
  crit_rate: 0.25
  ied_pct: 1.00
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.20 }
